---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const html = '<p>Small law firms adopt cash balance plans because partners have different ages, different draws, and a shared annoyance with the 401(k) cap. A cash balance formula can give a larger pay credit to an older partner and a smaller one to a younger partner, within nondiscrimination rules. It cannot give a senior partner a private tax shelter that ignores associates.</p>\n<p>Two practical problems show up every year. First, guaranteed payments and W-2 wages get mixed up in conversation. The plan sees compensation the document defines, which has to match how the firm actually pays people. Second, a lateral hire mid-year changes the test. Read <a href="/staff-cost">staff cost</a> and <a href="/fees">who does the valuation</a>.</p>\n<p>The 2026 defined-benefit dollar limit is <strong>$290,000</strong> of annual benefit, per the <a href="https://www.irs.gov/retirement-plans/plan-participant-employee/retirement-topics-defined-benefit-plan-benefit-limits">IRS</a>. It is not a contribution. Illustrations belong on <a href="/illustrations">the illustrations page</a>. For the firm’s existing 401(k), including Roth catch-up for high earners in 2026, ask the recordkeeper; that rule is not a cash balance rule. Background is in <a href="https://www.irs.gov/newsroom/401k-limit-increases-to-24500-for-2026-ira-limit-increases-to-7500">IR-2025-111</a>.</p>\n<img src="/images/guides/attorneys.jpg" alt="Attorneys in a conference room" class="mt-6 h-80 w-full rounded-3xl object-cover" />';
---
<Base title="Small law firms. | Savant Pensions">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">Attorneys</p>
    <h1>Small law firms.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Partners rarely want the same credit. The plan does not have to pretend they do.</p>
    <div class="guide" set:html={html} />
  </section>
</Base>
